{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Declaring a macro","anchor":"Declaring-a-macro","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro","doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetRecordMacro"]},{"title":"Diagnostics","anchor":"Diagnostics","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The expansion behind every linker-set macro, for clients that declare a kind and a macro of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their own.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","title":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport","externalID":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry(kind:)"},{"type":"text","text":" takes its kind as an argument. A client that registers one kind of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thing (routes, events, migrations) gives it a macro that fixes the kind instead, so its users"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route"},{"type":"text","text":" and never see a number. That takes three declarations."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The client’s compiler plugin, a ","type":"text"},{"code":".macro","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" target that depends on this module, names the kind:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import LinkerSetsMacroSupport","import SwiftCompilerPlugin","","@main","struct RoutesMacrosPlugin: CompilerPlugin {","    let providingMacros: [any Macro.Type] = [RouteMacro.self]","}","","public enum RouteMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x726F_7574 }  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The client’s library declares the macro, the same kind, and the read of the set. It depends on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSets and re-exports it, because the expansion calls LinkerSets’ ","type":"text"},{"code":"#linkerSetRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"users’ files:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Route() = #externalMacro(module: \"RoutesMacros\", type: \"RouteMacro\")","","extension Endpoints {","    public static var all: [Endpoint] {","        LinkerSet<Endpoint>(kind: .routes).values","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Its users then register routes and read them through the library:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["enum Endpoints {","    @Route static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","}","","let endpoints = Endpoints.all"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What the re-export exposes","anchor":"What-the-re-export-exposes"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Route static let home = ...","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" expands, in the user’s file, to one call:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"#linkerSetRecord(kind: 0x726F7574, storing: Routes.home)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". That macro, which LinkerSets declares,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expands in turn to the record itself, one declaration per object format, naming","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSetsRuntime.LinkerSetRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". So the user’s file has to see LinkerSets. With","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@_exported import LinkerSets","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the client’s library, importing the client is enough. With a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plain or ","type":"text"},{"code":"public import","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", every user’s file fails to compile with “no macro named","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"‘linkerSetRecord’” until it imports LinkerSets itself. The compile tests in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tests\/CompileFailures","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"ExportingClientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ImportingClientUser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ImportingClientUserImportingLinkerSets","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") check each case.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"So every file that imports the client also sees ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetKind"},{"text":" and anything","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"public the client adds to them. A kind constant doesn’t need to be public: the macro writes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"kind as a number, so users’ files never name the constant. Keep it internal and give users the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values through the client’s own API, as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Endpoints.all"},{"text":" does above. A user can still read the set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by its number, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)"},{"text":"; an internal constant only keeps it out of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"autocomplete and out of the client’s public API.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro","type":"reference"},{"text":" writes the same record ","type":"text"},{"code":"@LinkerSetEntry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes, in the same section, and its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"diagnostics name the client’s attribute (","type":"text"},{"code":"'@Route' applies to static members only","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). Each kind","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a set of its own, so two clients in one program never see each other’s records as long as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their kinds differ. Kind 0 is reserved, and the expansion refuses it.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Registering types","anchor":"Registering-types"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A macro attached to a struct, enum, class or actor stores the type’s metatype. To read the types","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a protocol they share, without casting, the plugin names that protocol in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/requiredConformance(of:)","isActive":true},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Events.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record then holds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type"},{"type":"text","text":", read with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values"},{"type":"text","text":". A type that doesn’t conform fails to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compile where it’s declared: “cannot convert value of type ‘NotAnEvent.Type’ to type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"‘any AnalyticsEvent.Type’”. Qualify the protocol with its module so a type of the same name at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the use site can’t stand in for it. Without a required protocol, a type’s record holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Any.Type"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A registered type can be nested in another from swift-syntax 600 on. Before 600 a macro can’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"see where its declaration sits, so the type must be declared at file scope."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A macro that takes its kind as an argument can return "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kindArgument(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kind(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Checking keys are unique","anchor":"Checking-keys-are-unique"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A macro can give each declaration a key that no other record of its kind in the same executable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or library may share, in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/uniqueKey(of:attribute:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". The expansion then adds a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"function whose symbol is named for the kind and the key, and a second declaration with the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key fails to compile in one module, or to link across modules:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func uniqueKey(of declaration: some DeclSyntaxProtocol, attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> String? {","        declaration.asProtocol(NamedDeclSyntax.self)?.name.text","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A macro whose users write the key returns ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/uniqueKeyArgument(of:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", which reads a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uniqueKey:"},{"text":" string literal. An empty key, and a key on a member of a private type, are refused","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with diagnostics of their own. The check reaches one linked image only; LinkerSets’ guide to unique","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keys shows each linker’s message and the limits.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Declaring the kind once","anchor":"Declaring-the-kind-once"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin returns the kind from ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kind(of:)"},{"text":" and the library reads the set by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, so the number appears twice, and a mismatch shows only at run time, as an empty set. To write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it once, put it in a module of its own that depends on nothing, and have both import it:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["\/\/ RoutesKind","public enum RouteKind {","    public static let rawValue: UInt32 = 0x726F_7574  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"code":["\/\/ RoutesMacros, the plugin","public enum RouteMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { RouteKind.rawValue }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"code":["\/\/ Routes, the library","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: RouteKind.rawValue)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The package lists the module among both targets’ dependencies:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".macro(name: \"RoutesMacros\", dependencies: [\"RoutesKind\", ...])"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".target(name: \"Routes\", dependencies: [\"RoutesKind\", \"RoutesMacros\", ...])"},{"text":". SwiftPM builds it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for the host for the plugin and for the target for the library.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Writing records without depending on LinkerSets","anchor":"Writing-records-without-depending-on-LinkerSets"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A module that uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry"},{"type":"text","text":" depends on LinkerSets, which builds LinkerSets’ own plugin,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"LinkerSetsMacros, and swift-syntax with it. A module that only writes a few records, such as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events of one feature, can skip that. A client with a plugin of its own declares two macros there:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an entry macro that takes the kind as an argument, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry"},{"type":"text","text":" does, and a record macro"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of its own under a different name, which the entry macro’s expansion calls in place of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#linkerSetRecord"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":["\/\/ DiscoveryMacros, the plugin","@main","struct DiscoveryMacrosPlugin: CompilerPlugin {","    let providingMacros: [any Macro.Type] = [DiscoverableMacro.self, DiscoverableRecordMacro.self]","}","","public enum DiscoverableMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) throws -> UInt32 {","        try kindArgument(of: attribute)","    }","","    public static var recordMacroName: String { \"discoverableRecord\" }","}","","public enum DiscoverableRecordMacro: DeclarationMacro {","    public static func expansion(","        of node: some FreestandingMacroExpansionSyntax,","        in context: some MacroExpansionContext","    ) throws -> [DeclSyntax] {","        try LinkerSetRecordMacro.expansion(of: node, in: context)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The library declares both and re-exports LinkerSetsRuntime, whose names the record uses:"}]},{"code":["\/\/ Discovery, the library","@_exported import LinkerSetsRuntime","","@attached(peer)","public macro Discoverable(kind: UInt32) = #externalMacro(module: \"DiscoveryMacros\", type: \"DiscoverableMacro\")","","@freestanding(declaration)","public macro discoverableRecord<Value>(kind: UInt32, storing value: Value) = #externalMacro(module: \"DiscoveryMacros\", type: \"DiscoverableRecordMacro\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A module that writes records then depends on "},{"code":"Discovery","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"LinkerSetsRuntime","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", not on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"LinkerSets, and writes "},{"code":"@Discoverable(kind: 0x7365_7373)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" where it would have written"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"@LinkerSetEntry(kind: 0x7365_7373)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Its build holds the client’s plugin, which already"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"needs swift-syntax, and not LinkerSetsMacros. The record macro’s name must differ from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"linkerSetRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", because a module that imports both LinkerSets and the client couldn’t choose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between two macros of the same name."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Testing the expansion","anchor":"Testing-the-expansion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A client’s expansion tests pin one line per record, the ","type":"text"},{"code":"#linkerSetRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["assertMacroExpansion(","    \"\"\"","    enum Endpoints {","        @Route","        static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","    }","    \"\"\",","    expandedSource: \"\"\"","    enum Endpoints {","        static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","","        #linkerSetRecord(kind: 0x726F7574, storing: Endpoints.home)","    }","    \"\"\",","    macroSpecs: [\"Route\": MacroSpec(type: RouteMacro.self)],","    failureHandler: { Issue.record(\"\\($0.message)\") }",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"assertMacroExpansion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" expands only the macros in its table, so the call stays as written, and it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads the same on every swift-syntax from 600 on. The record behind it, one declaration per object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, belongs to LinkerSets and changes when LinkerSets adds a format. A test that wants it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anyway adds "},{"code":"\"linkerSetRecord\": MacroSpec(type: LinkerSetRecordMacro.self)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to the table. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declaration at file scope expands to the call inside a private enum of its own, whose name comes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the context’s unique names ("},{"code":"__macro_local_15linkerSetRecordfMu_","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Writing the expansion yourself","anchor":"Writing-the-expansion-yourself"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro"},{"text":" supplies the peer ","type":"text"},{"code":"expansion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A macro that needs more writes its own and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"calls ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/recordPeers(of:providingPeersOf:in:)"},{"text":" from it for the record. That’s how","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a macro adds the conformance as well, so its users write ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event struct Login {}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" without naming","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the protocol. The macro takes an extension role beside the peer:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro, ExtensionMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Events.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","","    \/\/ The record, as a peer.","    public static func expansion(","        of node: AttributeSyntax,","        providingPeersOf declaration: some DeclSyntaxProtocol,","        in context: some MacroExpansionContext","    ) throws -> [DeclSyntax] {","        try recordPeers(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context)","    }","","    \/\/ The conformance the record requires, as an extension.","    public static func expansion(","        of node: AttributeSyntax,","        attachedTo declaration: some DeclGroupSyntax,","        providingExtensionsOf type: some TypeSyntaxProtocol,","        conformingTo protocols: [TypeSyntax],","        in context: some MacroExpansionContext","    ) throws -> [ExtensionDeclSyntax] {","        [try ExtensionDeclSyntax(\"extension \\(type.trimmed): Events.AnalyticsEvent {}\")]","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The library declares the macro with both roles:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["@attached(peer)","@attached(extension, conformances: AnalyticsEvent)","public macro Event() = #externalMacro(module: \"EventsMacros\", type: \"EventMacro\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A type can then carry data of its own through the protocol (a schema, a name) while the record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holds only its metatype, read as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Skipping a record instead of refusing it","anchor":"Skipping-a-record-instead-of-refusing-it"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The expansion refuses what a record can’t hold with an error. A macro that would rather skip some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of those (a generic event that its library lists by hand, say) asks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/refusal(of:providingPeersOf:in:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" first. It returns a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" whose "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic\/reason-swift.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" says why, and whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic\/node","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is where to report it, or "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when the declaration can hold a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record:"}]},{"code":["public static func expansion(","    of node: AttributeSyntax,","    providingPeersOf declaration: some DeclSyntaxProtocol,","    in context: some MacroExpansionContext",") throws -> [DeclSyntax] {","    if let refusal = try refusal(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context),","       refusal.reason == .genericType {","        context.diagnose(Diagnostic(node: refusal.node, message: GenericEventNote()))","        return []","    }","    return try recordPeers(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every other refusal still reaches "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/recordPeers(of:providingPeersOf:in:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws it. Where a declaration sits (in a function’s body, a protocol or a generic type) is seen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from swift-syntax 600 on; before it those three aren’t returned, and the compiler refuses them in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the expansion."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A member declared in an extension of a generic type is refused only when the extension shows the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type is generic: by naming generic arguments ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"extension Box<Int>"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"extension [Int]"},{"type":"text","text":") or with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"where"},{"type":"text","text":" clause. A plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"extension Box"},{"type":"text","text":" of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"struct Box<T>"},{"type":"text","text":" reads like an extension of any other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type, because the macro sees the extension’s syntax and not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Box"},{"type":"text","text":"’s declaration. No refusal is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returned for it, and the compiler fails inside the expansion with “static stored properties not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"supported in generic types”. A client macro whose users might write one can say so in its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"docs."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://LinkerSetsMacroSupport/documentation/LinkerSetsMacroSupport/LinkerSetMacro/uniqueKeyArgument(of:)":{"title":"uniqueKeyArgument(of:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The attribute’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uniqueKey:"},{"type":"text","text":" argument, a string literal, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when it has none."}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"uniqueKeyArgument","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"of","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AttributeSyntax","preciseIdentifier":"s:11SwiftSyntax09AttributeB0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/uniqueKeyArgument(of:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport\/linkersetmacro\/uniquekeyargument(of:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://LinkerSetsMacroSupport/documentation/LinkerSetsMacroSupport/LinkerSetMacro/refusal(of:providingPeersOf:in:)":{"title":"refusal(of:providingPeersOf:in:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/refusal(of:providingPeersOf:in:)","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport\/linkersetmacro\/refusal(of:providingpeersof:in:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"declaration"},{"type":"text","text":" can’t hold a record, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when it can: the checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/recordPeers(of:providingPeersOf:in:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes of the declaration and of where it sits,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without writing anything."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":